WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.640
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:02.950
JENNY BROWN: There are a
number of business benefits

00:00:02.950 --> 00:00:05.920
that go along with moving
applications to the Cloud,

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:09.070
and certain workloads
are easier than others.

00:00:09.070 --> 00:00:11.560
Apps running in the
Cloud require a variety

00:00:11.560 --> 00:00:16.540
of storage solutions, including
block, file, or object storage,

00:00:16.540 --> 00:00:19.120
and in some cases,
a combination.

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.820
Ultimately, you need to
find the appropriate storage

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:24.130
architecture for
each need because you

00:00:24.130 --> 00:00:27.910
can't rewrite every app to
use one type of storage,

00:00:27.910 --> 00:00:29.710
nor should you.

00:00:29.710 --> 00:00:32.680
From a Cloud ops
viewpoint, where you store

00:00:32.680 --> 00:00:35.380
is just as important
as what you store.

00:00:35.380 --> 00:00:39.100
If you choose to use storage
options from multiple companies

00:00:39.100 --> 00:00:41.200
or work with
third-party providers,

00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:44.560
you'll be juggling multiple
UIs, setup requirements,

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:46.240
and access points--

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:49.810
not to mention, setting
up multiple IM, CMEK,

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:52.270
and other security
policies results

00:00:52.270 --> 00:00:54.970
in context switching
that can seriously

00:00:54.970 --> 00:00:57.160
impact your team's efficiency.

00:00:57.160 --> 00:00:59.470
And let's be honest,
your folks would love

00:00:59.470 --> 00:01:01.840
to have their weekends back.

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:05.470
Fortunately, Google Cloud
offers you a full portfolio

00:01:05.470 --> 00:01:07.960
of block, file,
and object storage

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:12.400
to choose from, including NFS
storage solutions, so you don't

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.370
compromise on an SLA
or business value

00:01:15.370 --> 00:01:18.380
that you're delivering
to your organization.

00:01:18.380 --> 00:01:20.350
And if you're looking
for file storage,

00:01:20.350 --> 00:01:23.890
we have multiple options
to best fit your needs.

00:01:23.890 --> 00:01:27.040
For a quick overview of the
Filestore product family,

00:01:27.040 --> 00:01:31.310
we have Filestore Basic, which
is built for many applications,

00:01:31.310 --> 00:01:34.000
including test
and dev workloads.

00:01:34.000 --> 00:01:37.450
Filestore High Scale is
excellent for larger storage

00:01:37.450 --> 00:01:40.960
capacity requirements and
higher performance requirements

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:45.310
that many HPC applications
need, like genomic sequencing

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:47.830
or financial trading analytics.

00:01:47.830 --> 00:01:51.220
Filestore Enterprise is
designed for critical business

00:01:51.220 --> 00:01:54.880
applications, like SAP
and other use cases, that

00:01:54.880 --> 00:01:57.820
also require high availability.

00:01:57.820 --> 00:02:01.660
And having a simple, trusted,
and streamlined place to manage

00:02:01.660 --> 00:02:04.570
these settings and get
things set up cannot be

00:02:04.570 --> 00:02:06.190
underestimated.

00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:10.180
Google Cloud gives you a simple,
yet powerful, user interface

00:02:10.180 --> 00:02:14.410
to provision storage capacity
for applications utilizing NFS.

00:02:14.410 --> 00:02:16.630
And if you're someone
that likes coding,

00:02:16.630 --> 00:02:19.240
we have a single set
of Filestore APIs

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:23.050
you can use across the
entire Filestore family.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:26.230
And for those who need to deploy
business-critical applications

00:02:26.230 --> 00:02:29.050
in the Cloud, with many of
the traditional enterprise

00:02:29.050 --> 00:02:33.400
features, like high availability
and integrated data protection,

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:36.490
we've built
Filestore Enterprise.

00:02:36.490 --> 00:02:38.350
Imagine having
the protection you

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.500
need but with a Cloud-native
and fully-managed storage

00:02:41.500 --> 00:02:44.530
service that has a
regional availability SLA

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.230
and file system snapshots.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.410
Only in the Cloud can your
data be seamlessly replicated

00:02:50.410 --> 00:02:52.480
to multiple zones
within a region,

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:56.200
all with a simplified,
single point of access.

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:58.330
And with Filestore
Snapshots, you

00:02:58.330 --> 00:03:00.940
can rest assured that
any and all of your data

00:03:00.940 --> 00:03:05.380
can be recovered within minutes
if the unthinkable happens.

00:03:05.380 --> 00:03:08.560
For example, a Canadian
financial services company

00:03:08.560 --> 00:03:12.220
moved its core SAP banking
systems to Google Cloud

00:03:12.220 --> 00:03:15.160
as it digitally transformed
its operations in order

00:03:15.160 --> 00:03:17.870
to improve its
client experiences.

00:03:17.870 --> 00:03:20.050
However, they
couldn't compromise

00:03:20.050 --> 00:03:22.420
with a nonresilient
storage solution.

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:25.420
High availability is of
the utmost importance

00:03:25.420 --> 00:03:28.630
for their mission-critical
SAP systems.

00:03:28.630 --> 00:03:31.480
And then there's a leading
travel reservation company

00:03:31.480 --> 00:03:34.420
that underwent an IT
modernization initiative

00:03:34.420 --> 00:03:37.450
and moved critical
applications to the Cloud.

00:03:37.450 --> 00:03:40.720
They chose Filestore
Enterprise to store and protect

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:43.630
their information,
ensuring their Cloud ops

00:03:43.630 --> 00:03:46.810
and their users could recover
any of that information

00:03:46.810 --> 00:03:48.700
when needed.

00:03:48.700 --> 00:03:52.360
No matter the demands of your
architecture or industry,

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.150
Google Cloud has a
comprehensive, trusted

00:03:55.150 --> 00:04:00.610
portfolio of block, file, and
object storage to choose from.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.500
And regardless of which
solution fits your needs,

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:08.470
you can keep things simple
with the unified Admin console.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:11.260
To learn more about
Filestore Enterprise or any

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.660
of our Filestore
solutions, check out

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:18.640
cloud.google.com/filestore
and head to the console

00:04:18.640 --> 00:04:22.089
to provision your own Filestore
Enterprise instance in just

00:04:22.089 --> 00:04:23.530
a few clicks today.

00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.880
